# Keep the build context free of artifacts produced by a local build.
#
# Without this file, `COPY . redis-cluster-proxy` copies the object files and
# the binary compiled for the build host. In a multi-platform buildx build
# `make` sees them as up to date and tries to link them for the target
# platform, which fails with:
#
#   ld: adlist.o: Relocations in generic ELF (EM: 183)
#   ld: adlist.o: error adding symbols: file in wrong format
#
# (183 is EM_AARCH64). The `.git` directory is intentionally kept: the build
# uses it to stamp the commit/branch reported by `PROXY INFO`.
**/*.o
**/*.a
**/redis-cluster-proxy
**/.make-*
**/Makefile.dep
**/*.dSYM
src/release.h
release.h
release
test/tmp
.DS_Store
